# BenQ Projector Driver (RS232 Command Control protocol)
#
# Controls BenQ projectors that speak BenQ's published "RS232 Command
# Control" ASCII protocol, over the network (TCP 8000) or a direct
# RS-232 line. Commands are key=value tokens framed by an asterisk and
# a hash, wrapped in carriage returns:
#   SET     <CR>*pow=on#<CR>
#   QUERY   <CR>*pow=?#<CR>
#   REPLY   *POW=ON#
# Commands are case-insensitive; replies vary in case by model (some
# echo the lowercase command back before answering, some answer in
# uppercase), so every response pattern here matches case-insensitively
# and normalizes to lowercase canonical tokens. Replies are terminated
# by the '#' itself — trailing CR/LF after '#' is not consistent across
# the family (some units append CRLF, some a NUL, some nothing), so the
# driver frames on '#' and strips the residue. Some firmware also emits
# a '>' prompt character; it is ignored by the unanchored matchers.
#
# Echo caveat: many units echo the command they received before (or
# instead of) the confirmation reply. A set-command echo is textually
# identical to its confirmation modulo case, so the driver treats the
# echo as the acknowledgement; if the device then rejects the command
# ("*Block item#"), the optimistic state is corrected on the next poll.
#
# Push vs poll: POLL-ONLY. The protocol is strictly request/response —
# BenQ's control guides define no subscription, notification, or event
# mechanism. The driver polls the documented Read commands and pulls
# model name + MAC address once on connect.
#
# Standby: with the projector off, most commands answer "*Block item#".
# Power on/off and the power query keep working. For LAN control in
# standby, Standby Settings > Network must be On (the standby_network
# device setting / *standbynet# command).
#
# Errors: "*Illegal format#" (bad syntax), "*Unsupported item#" (valid
# command the model doesn't implement — benign, per-model Support
# varies), "*Block item#" (valid command refused in the current state,
# e.g. most things during standby or warm-up).
#
# Protocol reference: BenQ "Projector RS232 Command Control Installation
# Guide" (published per model on BenQ's support site; the command table
# is shared across the projector line, with a per-model Support column).

id: benq_projector
name: BenQ Projector
manufacturer: BenQ
category: projector
version: 1.0.0
author: OpenAVC
description: >-
  Controls BenQ projectors using BenQ's RS232 Command Control protocol
  over the network (TCP 8000) or direct RS-232. Covers the install and
  large-venue families (LK / LU / LH / PU / PW / PX / L series) and the
  wider BenQ line that shares the same command table. Power, source
  select, volume and mute, picture mode, picture adjustment steps,
  color temperature, aspect ratio, blank, freeze, OSD menu navigation,
  light source mode and custom light level, lens memories, and
  installer settings (direct power on, quick auto search, high
  altitude, standby network). Polls for status.

source_url: https://esupportdownload.benq.com/esupport/PROJECTOR/Control%20Protocols/LK952/LK952_RS232%20Control%20Guide_0_Windows10_Windows7_Windows8.pdf
tags: [projector, benq, rs232, lan-control, laser, install]
verified: false
simulated: true
ports: [8000]
min_platform_version: "0.23.0"
compatible_models:
  - manufacturer: BenQ
    models:
      - LK952
      - LK953ST
      - LK990
      - LU950
      - LU951
      - LU951ST
      - LU9715
      - LU9750
      - LU9800
      - LU9915
      - L6000
      - PU9530
      - PW9520
      - PX9510
      - EW805ST
    confidence: untested
    notes: >-
      Each of these models has a published BenQ RS232 Command Control
      guide with the same command grammar. The guides carry a per-model
      Support column — a command a given model doesn't implement answers
      "*Unsupported item#", which the driver ignores. Most other BenQ
      network/serial-controllable projectors (including the home-cinema
      W series) share the same protocol and are expected to work.

transport: tcp
transports: [tcp, serial]
# BenQ replies are terminated by the '#' token itself; trailing CR/LF
# after it varies by model (sometimes absent entirely), so '#' is the
# only framing byte every unit honors.
delimiter: "#"

help:
  overview: >-
    BenQ projectors speaking the BenQ RS232 Command Control protocol —
    the install / large-venue LK, LU, LH, PU, PW, PX, and L series and
    most other BenQ models with a LAN or RS-232 control port. Power,
    source, audio, picture controls, blank/freeze, OSD navigation,
    light source (lamp/laser) modes, lens memories, and installer
    settings. Polls every 30 seconds. For commands not exposed here,
    use Send Raw Command with the command table from your model's
    "RS232 Command Control Installation Guide" on BenQ's support site.
  setup: >-
    1. Network control: connect the projector's LAN port, note its IP
       address from the Network menu, and add it here with TCP port
       8000.
    2. To keep network control available while the projector is off,
       turn on Standby Settings > Network on the projector (or write
       the Standby Network device setting once connected).
    3. Serial control: connect the RS-232 port (or a serial bridge) at
       the baud rate shown in the projector's OSD (9600 default on most
       models), 8 data bits, no parity, 1 stop bit.
    4. Volume and custom light level ranges vary by model — check your
       model's guide or the OSD for the valid span.
  connection: >-
    If the projector is powered off, its LAN control port only answers
    when Standby Settings > Network is On in the projector's menu.

discovery:
  # Active fingerprint: the model-name query on TCP 8000 answers
  # *MODELNAME=<model># — a deterministic, vendor-unique grammar. The
  # extract skips the '?' of a command echo so the captured model is
  # the real reply. Port 8000 is in the generic-port denylist, so no
  # port_open hint; OUI + manufacturer alias let the projector surface
  # from ARP/NetBIOS sweeps. BenQ models also answer PJLink on 4352 —
  # the pjlink_class1 cross-vendor fingerprint demotes to this driver
  # via the manufacturer alias.
  #   Refs:
  #     BenQ LK952 RS232 Command Control Installation Guide (LAN: TCP 8000)
  #     maclookup.app/vendors/benq-corporation (OUI 80:65:E9)
  tcp_probe:
    port: 8000
    send_ascii: "\r*modelname=?#\r"
    expect_regex: '(?i:\*modelname=)'
    extract_manufacturer: "BenQ"
    extract:
      model:
        regex: '(?i:\*modelname=([^?#][^#]*)#)'
        group: 1
  oui:
    - "80:65:e9"
  manufacturer_alias:
    - "benq"
    - "benq corporation"

default_config:
  host: ""
  port: 8000
  poll_interval: 30
  inter_command_delay: 0.1
  baudrate: 9600
  parity: "N"
  bytesize: 8
  stopbits: 1

config_schema:
  host:
    type: string
    required: true
    label: IP Address
    description: Projector IP address (Network menu). TCP control uses port 8000.
  port:
    type: integer
    default: 8000
    label: TCP Port
    description: Default 8000 for BenQ LAN control
  poll_interval:
    type: integer
    default: 30
    min: 5
    label: Poll Interval (sec)
  inter_command_delay:
    type: number
    default: 0.1
    label: Inter-Command Delay (sec)
  baudrate:
    type: integer
    default: 9600
    label: Baud Rate (serial)
    description: Match the projector's OSD baud rate setting (9600 default on most models)

state_variables:
  power:
    type: enum
    values: ["off", "on"]
    label: Power
    control: true
    help: "Power state from *pow=?#. During warm-up/cool-down the projector answers *Block item# and the last known state holds."
  source:
    type: enum
    values: [rgb, rgb2, rgb3, ypbr, ypbr2, dvia, dvid, hdmi, hdmi2, hdmi3, vid, svid, network, usbdisplay, usbreader, hdbaset, dp, sdi]
    label: Source
    control: true
    help: "Selected input from *sour=?#, normalized to the lowercase wire token (hdmi, hdbaset, rgb, ...)."
  volume:
    type: integer
    label: Volume
    control: true
    help: "Speaker/audio-out volume from *vol=?#. Range varies by model."
  mute:
    type: boolean
    label: Mute
    control: true
    help: "Audio mute state from *mute=?#."
  picture_mode:
    type: enum
    values: [dynamic, preset, srgb, bright, livingroom, game, cine, std, football, footballbt, dicom, thx, silence, dci-p3, vivid, infographic, user1, user2, user3, isfday, isfnight, threed]
    label: Picture Mode
    help: "Active picture mode from *appmod=?# (preset = Presentation). Available modes vary by model."
  aspect:
    type: enum
    values: ["4:3", "16:9", "16:10", "16:6", auto, real, lbox, wide, anam, anam2.35, anam16:9]
    label: Aspect Ratio
    help: "Aspect ratio from *asp=?#."
  color_temp:
    type: enum
    values: [warmer, warm, normal, cool, cooler, native]
    label: Color Temperature
    help: "Color temperature from *ct=?# (native = lamp native)."
  contrast:
    type: integer
    label: Contrast
    help: "Contrast value from *con=?#. The protocol only steps it up/down; range varies by model."
  brightness:
    type: integer
    label: Brightness
    help: "Brightness value from *bri=?#. The protocol only steps it up/down; range varies by model."
  color:
    type: integer
    label: Color Saturation
    help: "Color value from *color=?#. The protocol only steps it up/down; range varies by model."
  sharpness:
    type: integer
    label: Sharpness
    help: "Sharpness value from *sharp=?#. The protocol only steps it up/down; range varies by model."
  blank:
    type: boolean
    label: Blank
    control: true
    help: "Picture blank state from *blank=?#."
  freeze:
    type: boolean
    label: Freeze
    help: "Image freeze state from *freeze=?#."
  light_mode:
    type: enum
    values: [lnor, eco, seco, seco2, seco3, dimming, custom]
    label: Light Source Mode
    help: "Lamp / laser light source mode from *lampm=?#: lnor=Normal, eco=Eco, seco=SmartEco, dimming=Dimming, custom=Custom."
  light_level:
    type: integer
    label: Custom Light Level
    help: "Light level for Custom light mode from *lampcustom=?#. Range varies by model."
  light_hours:
    type: integer
    label: Light Source Hours
    help: "Lamp / light source usage hours from *ltim=?#."
  position:
    type: enum
    values: [ft, re, rc, fc]
    label: Projector Position
    help: "Mounting position from *pp=?#: ft=Front Table, re=Rear Table, rc=Rear Ceiling, fc=Front Ceiling."
  direct_power_on:
    type: enum
    values: ["on", "off"]
    label: Direct Power On
    help: "Whether the projector powers on as soon as mains is applied (*directpower=?#)."
  quick_auto_search:
    type: enum
    values: ["on", "off"]
    label: Quick Auto Search
    help: "Automatic input search state from *QAS=?#."
  high_altitude:
    type: enum
    values: ["on", "off"]
    label: High Altitude Mode
    help: "High altitude fan mode from *Highaltitude=?#."
  standby_network:
    type: enum
    values: ["on", "off"]
    label: Network in Standby
    help: "Whether the LAN control port stays active in standby (*standbynet=?#). Must be on for network control of a powered-off projector."
  model_name:
    type: string
    label: Model
    help: "Projector model reported by *modelname=?#."
  mac_address:
    type: string
    label: MAC Address
    help: "LAN MAC address reported by *macaddr=?#."

commands:
  # ── Power ──
  power_on:
    label: Power On
    send: "\r*pow=on#\r"
    help: Turn the projector on. Commands during warm-up answer *Block item#.

  power_off:
    label: Power Off
    send: "\r*pow=off#\r"

  # ── Source ──
  set_source:
    label: Select Source
    send: "\r*sour={source}#\r"
    help: Select an input. Sources a given model lacks answer *Unsupported item#.
    params:
      source:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: Source
        values:
          - { value: hdmi, label: "HDMI 1" }
          - { value: hdmi2, label: "HDMI 2" }
          - { value: hdmi3, label: "HDMI 3" }
          - { value: hdbaset, label: "HDBaseT" }
          - { value: dp, label: "DisplayPort" }
          - { value: sdi, label: "3G-SDI" }
          - { value: RGB, label: "Computer 1 (RGB/YPbPr)" }
          - { value: RGB2, label: "Computer 2" }
          - { value: RGB3, label: "Computer 3" }
          - { value: ypbr, label: "Component" }
          - { value: ypbr2, label: "Component 2" }
          - { value: dviA, label: "DVI-A" }
          - { value: dvid, label: "DVI-D" }
          - { value: vid, label: "Composite" }
          - { value: svid, label: "S-Video" }
          - { value: network, label: "Network" }
          - { value: usbdisplay, label: "USB Display" }
          - { value: usbreader, label: "USB Reader" }

  # ── Audio ──
  mute_on:
    label: Mute On
    send: "\r*mute=on#\r"

  mute_off:
    label: Mute Off
    send: "\r*mute=off#\r"

  volume_up:
    label: Volume Up
    send: "\r*vol=+#\r"

  volume_down:
    label: Volume Down
    send: "\r*vol=-#\r"

  set_volume:
    label: Set Volume
    send: "\r*vol={level}#\r"
    help: Set an absolute volume level. Valid range varies by model.
    params:
      level:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: Volume Level

  # ── Picture ──
  set_picture_mode:
    label: Set Picture Mode
    send: "\r*appmod={mode}#\r"
    help: Select a picture mode. Modes a given model lacks answer *Unsupported item#.
    params:
      mode:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: Picture Mode
        values:
          - { value: preset, label: "Presentation" }
          - { value: bright, label: "Bright" }
          - { value: srgb, label: "sRGB" }
          - { value: vivid, label: "Vivid" }
          - { value: dicom, label: "DICOM SIM" }
          - { value: cine, label: "Cinema" }
          - { value: dynamic, label: "Dynamic" }
          - { value: std, label: "Standard" }
          - { value: livingroom, label: "Living Room" }
          - { value: game, label: "Game" }
          - { value: football, label: "Football" }
          - { value: footballbt, label: "Football Bright" }
          - { value: thx, label: "THX" }
          - { value: silence, label: "Silence" }
          - { value: dci-p3, label: "DCI-P3" }
          - { value: infographic, label: "Infographic" }
          - { value: user1, label: "User 1" }
          - { value: user2, label: "User 2" }
          - { value: user3, label: "User 3" }
          - { value: isfday, label: "ISF Day" }
          - { value: isfnight, label: "ISF Night" }
          - { value: threed, label: "3D" }

  contrast_up:
    label: Contrast +
    send: "\r*con=+#\r"

  contrast_down:
    label: Contrast -
    send: "\r*con=-#\r"

  brightness_up:
    label: Brightness +
    send: "\r*bri=+#\r"

  brightness_down:
    label: Brightness -
    send: "\r*bri=-#\r"

  color_up:
    label: Color +
    send: "\r*color=+#\r"

  color_down:
    label: Color -
    send: "\r*color=-#\r"

  sharpness_up:
    label: Sharpness +
    send: "\r*sharp=+#\r"

  sharpness_down:
    label: Sharpness -
    send: "\r*sharp=-#\r"

  set_color_temp:
    label: Set Color Temperature
    send: "\r*ct={temp}#\r"
    params:
      temp:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: Color Temperature
        values:
          - { value: warmer, label: "Warmer" }
          - { value: warm, label: "Warm" }
          - { value: normal, label: "Normal" }
          - { value: cool, label: "Cool" }
          - { value: cooler, label: "Cooler" }
          - { value: native, label: "Lamp Native" }

  set_aspect:
    label: Set Aspect Ratio
    send: "\r*asp={aspect}#\r"
    params:
      aspect:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: Aspect Ratio
        values:
          - { value: "AUTO", label: "Auto" }
          - { value: "4:3", label: "4:3" }
          - { value: "16:9", label: "16:9" }
          - { value: "16:10", label: "16:10" }
          - { value: "16:6", label: "16:6" }
          - { value: "REAL", label: "Real" }
          - { value: "LBOX", label: "Letterbox" }
          - { value: "WIDE", label: "Wide" }
          - { value: "ANAM", label: "Anamorphic" }
          - { value: "ANAM2.35", label: "Anamorphic 2.35:1" }
          - { value: "ANAM16:9", label: "Anamorphic 16:9" }

  auto_sync:
    label: Auto Sync
    send: "\r*auto#\r"
    help: Auto-adjust the image for analog computer sources.

  # ── Display ──
  blank_on:
    label: Blank On
    send: "\r*blank=on#\r"

  blank_off:
    label: Blank Off
    send: "\r*blank=off#\r"

  freeze_on:
    label: Freeze On
    send: "\r*freeze=on#\r"

  freeze_off:
    label: Freeze Off
    send: "\r*freeze=off#\r"

  # ── OSD menu navigation ──
  menu_on:
    label: Menu On
    send: "\r*menu=on#\r"

  menu_off:
    label: Menu Off
    send: "\r*menu=off#\r"

  menu_up:
    label: Menu Up
    send: "\r*up#\r"

  menu_down:
    label: Menu Down
    send: "\r*down#\r"

  menu_left:
    label: Menu Left
    send: "\r*left#\r"

  menu_right:
    label: Menu Right
    send: "\r*right#\r"

  menu_enter:
    label: Menu Enter / OK
    send: "\r*enter#\r"

  # ── Light source ──
  set_light_mode:
    label: Set Light Source Mode
    send: "\r*lampm={mode}#\r"
    params:
      mode:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: Light Source Mode
        values:
          - { value: lnor, label: "Normal" }
          - { value: eco, label: "Eco" }
          - { value: seco, label: "SmartEco" }
          - { value: seco2, label: "SmartEco 2" }
          - { value: seco3, label: "SmartEco 3" }
          - { value: dimming, label: "Dimming" }
          - { value: custom, label: "Custom" }

  set_light_level:
    label: Set Custom Light Level
    send: "\r*lampcustom={level}#\r"
    help: Light level used by the Custom light mode. Valid range varies by model.
    params:
      level:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: Light Level

  # ── Lens ──
  lens_memory_load:
    label: Load Lens Memory
    send: "\r*lensload=m{slot}#\r"
    help: Recall a stored lens position (models with powered lens memory).
    params:
      slot:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: Memory Slot
        min: 1
        max: 10

  lens_memory_save:
    label: Save Lens Memory
    send: "\r*lenssave=m{slot}#\r"
    params:
      slot:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: Memory Slot
        min: 1
        max: 10

  lens_reset_center:
    label: Reset Lens to Center
    send: "\r*lensreset=center#\r"

  digital_zoom_in:
    label: Digital Zoom In
    send: "\r*zoomI#\r"

  digital_zoom_out:
    label: Digital Zoom Out
    send: "\r*zoomO#\r"

  # ── Raw escape hatch ──
  send_command:
    label: Send Raw Command
    send: "\r{raw}\r"
    help: >-
      Send any command from your model's RS232 Command Control guide,
      including the asterisk and hash, e.g. "*pow=on#" or "*ltim=?#".
      The driver wraps it in carriage returns.
    params:
      raw:
        type: string
        required: true
        label: Raw Command
        pattern: '^\*[^#]+#$'

# Replies are *KEY=VALUE# in model-dependent case; the '#' delimiter is
# consumed by framing, so patterns match the bare *KEY=VALUE text
# case-insensitively and normalize enum tokens to lowercase. \b guards
# keep short tokens from matching longer ones (hdmi vs hdmi2, warm vs
# warmer, seco vs seco2).
responses:
  # ── Power ──
  - match: '(?i:\*pow=on\b)'
    set: { power: "on" }
  - match: '(?i:\*pow=off\b)'
    set: { power: "off" }

  # ── Source ──
  - match: '(?i:\*sour=rgb2\b)'
    set: { source: rgb2 }
  - match: '(?i:\*sour=rgb3\b)'
    set: { source: rgb3 }
  - match: '(?i:\*sour=rgb\b)'
    set: { source: rgb }
  - match: '(?i:\*sour=ypbr2\b)'
    set: { source: ypbr2 }
  - match: '(?i:\*sour=ypbr\b)'
    set: { source: ypbr }
  - match: '(?i:\*sour=dvia\b)'
    set: { source: dvia }
  - match: '(?i:\*sour=dvid\b)'
    set: { source: dvid }
  - match: '(?i:\*sour=hdmi2\b)'
    set: { source: hdmi2 }
  - match: '(?i:\*sour=hdmi3\b)'
    set: { source: hdmi3 }
  - match: '(?i:\*sour=hdmi\b)'
    set: { source: hdmi }
  - match: '(?i:\*sour=svid\b)'
    set: { source: svid }
  - match: '(?i:\*sour=vid\b)'
    set: { source: vid }
  - match: '(?i:\*sour=network\b)'
    set: { source: network }
  - match: '(?i:\*sour=usbdisplay\b)'
    set: { source: usbdisplay }
  - match: '(?i:\*sour=usbreader\b)'
    set: { source: usbreader }
  - match: '(?i:\*sour=hdbaset\b)'
    set: { source: hdbaset }
  - match: '(?i:\*sour=dp\b)'
    set: { source: dp }
  - match: '(?i:\*sour=sdi\b)'
    set: { source: sdi }

  # ── Audio ──
  - match: '(?i:\*mute=on\b)'
    set: { mute: "true" }
  - match: '(?i:\*mute=off\b)'
    set: { mute: "false" }
  - match: '(?i:\*vol=(\d+)\b)'
    set: { volume: "$1" }

  # ── Picture mode ──
  - match: '(?i:\*appmod=dynamic\b)'
    set: { picture_mode: dynamic }
  - match: '(?i:\*appmod=preset\b)'
    set: { picture_mode: preset }
  - match: '(?i:\*appmod=srgb\b)'
    set: { picture_mode: srgb }
  - match: '(?i:\*appmod=bright\b)'
    set: { picture_mode: bright }
  - match: '(?i:\*appmod=livingroom\b)'
    set: { picture_mode: livingroom }
  - match: '(?i:\*appmod=game\b)'
    set: { picture_mode: game }
  - match: '(?i:\*appmod=cine\b)'
    set: { picture_mode: cine }
  - match: '(?i:\*appmod=std\b)'
    set: { picture_mode: std }
  - match: '(?i:\*appmod=footballbt\b)'
    set: { picture_mode: footballbt }
  - match: '(?i:\*appmod=football\b)'
    set: { picture_mode: football }
  - match: '(?i:\*appmod=dicom\b)'
    set: { picture_mode: dicom }
  - match: '(?i:\*appmod=thx\b)'
    set: { picture_mode: thx }
  - match: '(?i:\*appmod=silence\b)'
    set: { picture_mode: silence }
  - match: '(?i:\*appmod=dci-p3\b)'
    set: { picture_mode: dci-p3 }
  - match: '(?i:\*appmod=vivid\b)'
    set: { picture_mode: vivid }
  - match: '(?i:\*appmod=infographic\b)'
    set: { picture_mode: infographic }
  - match: '(?i:\*appmod=user1\b)'
    set: { picture_mode: user1 }
  - match: '(?i:\*appmod=user2\b)'
    set: { picture_mode: user2 }
  - match: '(?i:\*appmod=user3\b)'
    set: { picture_mode: user3 }
  - match: '(?i:\*appmod=isfday\b)'
    set: { picture_mode: isfday }
  - match: '(?i:\*appmod=isfnight\b)'
    set: { picture_mode: isfnight }
  - match: '(?i:\*appmod=threed\b)'
    set: { picture_mode: threed }

  # ── Aspect ── (anam2.35 / anam16:9 listed before anam is not needed —
  # the \b guard already keeps 'anam' from matching them — but the
  # specific-first order costs nothing and reads clearer)
  - match: '(?i:\*asp=anam2\.35\b)'
    set: { aspect: anam2.35 }
  - match: '(?i:\*asp=anam16:9\b)'
    set: { aspect: anam16:9 }
  - match: '(?i:\*asp=anam\b)'
    set: { aspect: anam }
  - match: '(?i:\*asp=4:3\b)'
    set: { aspect: "4:3" }
  - match: '(?i:\*asp=16:9\b)'
    set: { aspect: "16:9" }
  - match: '(?i:\*asp=16:10\b)'
    set: { aspect: "16:10" }
  - match: '(?i:\*asp=16:6\b)'
    set: { aspect: "16:6" }
  - match: '(?i:\*asp=auto\b)'
    set: { aspect: auto }
  - match: '(?i:\*asp=real\b)'
    set: { aspect: real }
  - match: '(?i:\*asp=lbox\b)'
    set: { aspect: lbox }
  - match: '(?i:\*asp=wide\b)'
    set: { aspect: wide }

  # ── Color temperature ──
  - match: '(?i:\*ct=warmer\b)'
    set: { color_temp: warmer }
  - match: '(?i:\*ct=warm\b)'
    set: { color_temp: warm }
  - match: '(?i:\*ct=normal\b)'
    set: { color_temp: normal }
  - match: '(?i:\*ct=cooler\b)'
    set: { color_temp: cooler }
  - match: '(?i:\*ct=cool\b)'
    set: { color_temp: cool }
  - match: '(?i:\*ct=native\b)'
    set: { color_temp: native }

  # ── Picture values ──
  - match: '(?i:\*con=(-?\d+)\b)'
    set: { contrast: "$1" }
  - match: '(?i:\*bri=(-?\d+)\b)'
    set: { brightness: "$1" }
  - match: '(?i:\*color=(-?\d+)\b)'
    set: { color: "$1" }
  - match: '(?i:\*sharp=(-?\d+)\b)'
    set: { sharpness: "$1" }

  # ── Blank / freeze ──
  - match: '(?i:\*blank=on\b)'
    set: { blank: "true" }
  - match: '(?i:\*blank=off\b)'
    set: { blank: "false" }
  - match: '(?i:\*freeze=on\b)'
    set: { freeze: "true" }
  - match: '(?i:\*freeze=off\b)'
    set: { freeze: "false" }

  # ── Light source ──
  - match: '(?i:\*lampm=lnor\b)'
    set: { light_mode: lnor }
  - match: '(?i:\*lampm=eco\b)'
    set: { light_mode: eco }
  - match: '(?i:\*lampm=seco2\b)'
    set: { light_mode: seco2 }
  - match: '(?i:\*lampm=seco3\b)'
    set: { light_mode: seco3 }
  - match: '(?i:\*lampm=seco\b)'
    set: { light_mode: seco }
  - match: '(?i:\*lampm=dimming\b)'
    set: { light_mode: dimming }
  - match: '(?i:\*lampm=custom\b)'
    set: { light_mode: custom }
  - match: '(?i:\*lampcustom=(\d+)\b)'
    set: { light_level: "$1" }
  - match: '(?i:\*ltim=(\d+)\b)'
    set: { light_hours: "$1" }

  # ── Position ──
  - match: '(?i:\*pp=ft\b)'
    set: { position: ft }
  - match: '(?i:\*pp=re\b)'
    set: { position: re }
  - match: '(?i:\*pp=rc\b)'
    set: { position: rc }
  - match: '(?i:\*pp=fc\b)'
    set: { position: fc }

  # ── Installer settings ──
  - match: '(?i:\*directpower=on\b)'
    set: { direct_power_on: "on" }
  - match: '(?i:\*directpower=off\b)'
    set: { direct_power_on: "off" }
  - match: '(?i:\*qas=on\b)'
    set: { quick_auto_search: "on" }
  - match: '(?i:\*qas=off\b)'
    set: { quick_auto_search: "off" }
  - match: '(?i:\*highaltitude=on\b)'
    set: { high_altitude: "on" }
  - match: '(?i:\*highaltitude=off\b)'
    set: { high_altitude: "off" }
  - match: '(?i:\*standbynet=on\b)'
    set: { standby_network: "on" }
  - match: '(?i:\*standbynet=off\b)'
    set: { standby_network: "off" }

  # ── Identity ── ([^?#] skips the '?' of a query echo so only the
  # real reply value is captured)
  - match: '(?i:\*modelname=([^?#][^#]*))'
    set: { model_name: "$1" }
  - match: '(?i:\*macaddr=([0-9a-f:. -]*[0-9a-f]))'
    set: { mac_address: "$1" }

# Values the projector persists and reports back — dual-surfaced with
# the matching commands (same wire strings). Boolean-shaped settings use
# on/off enums because the wire tokens are the words, not 1/0. Volume
# and custom light level carry no min/max — the valid span is
# model-dependent and undocumented in the shared command table.
device_settings:
  volume:
    type: integer
    label: Volume
    help: "Speaker/audio-out volume (*vol=<n>#). Valid range varies by model."
    state_key: volume
    default: 5
    setup: false
    write:
      send: "\r*vol={value}#\r"
  light_mode:
    type: enum
    values:
      - { value: lnor, label: "Normal" }
      - { value: eco, label: "Eco" }
      - { value: seco, label: "SmartEco" }
      - { value: seco2, label: "SmartEco 2" }
      - { value: seco3, label: "SmartEco 3" }
      - { value: dimming, label: "Dimming" }
      - { value: custom, label: "Custom" }
    label: Light Source Mode
    help: "Lamp / laser light source mode (*lampm=<mode>#)."
    state_key: light_mode
    default: lnor
    setup: false
    write:
      send: "\r*lampm={value}#\r"
  light_level:
    type: integer
    label: Custom Light Level
    help: "Light level used by the Custom light mode (*lampcustom=<n>#). Valid range varies by model."
    state_key: light_level
    default: 100
    setup: false
    write:
      send: "\r*lampcustom={value}#\r"
  position:
    type: enum
    values:
      - { value: ft, label: "Front Table" }
      - { value: re, label: "Rear Table" }
      - { value: rc, label: "Rear Ceiling" }
      - { value: fc, label: "Front Ceiling" }
    label: Projector Position
    help: "Mounting position (*pp=<pos>#)."
    state_key: position
    default: ft
    setup: false
    write:
      send: "\r*pp={value}#\r"
  direct_power_on:
    type: enum
    values: ["on", "off"]
    label: Direct Power On
    help: "Power on as soon as mains is applied (*directpower=on|off#)."
    state_key: direct_power_on
    default: "off"
    setup: false
    write:
      send: "\r*directpower={value}#\r"
  quick_auto_search:
    type: enum
    values: ["on", "off"]
    label: Quick Auto Search
    help: "Automatically search inputs for a signal (*QAS=on|off#)."
    state_key: quick_auto_search
    default: "off"
    setup: false
    write:
      send: "\r*QAS={value}#\r"
  high_altitude:
    type: enum
    values: ["on", "off"]
    label: High Altitude Mode
    help: "High altitude fan mode (*Highaltitude=on|off#)."
    state_key: high_altitude
    default: "off"
    setup: false
    write:
      send: "\r*Highaltitude={value}#\r"
  standby_network:
    type: enum
    values: ["on", "off"]
    label: Network in Standby
    help: "Keep the LAN control port active in standby (*standbynet=on|off#). Required for network control of a powered-off projector."
    state_key: standby_network
    default: "on"
    setup: false
    write:
      send: "\r*standbynet={value}#\r"

quick_actions:
  - power_on
  - power_off
  - blank_on
  - blank_off

polling:
  queries:
    - "\r*pow=?#\r"
    - "\r*sour=?#\r"
    - "\r*vol=?#\r"
    - "\r*mute=?#\r"
    - "\r*appmod=?#\r"
    - "\r*asp=?#\r"
    - "\r*ct=?#\r"
    - "\r*con=?#\r"
    - "\r*bri=?#\r"
    - "\r*color=?#\r"
    - "\r*sharp=?#\r"
    - "\r*blank=?#\r"
    - "\r*freeze=?#\r"
    - "\r*lampm=?#\r"
    - "\r*lampcustom=?#\r"
    - "\r*ltim=?#\r"
    - "\r*pp=?#\r"
    - "\r*directpower=?#\r"
    - "\r*QAS=?#\r"
    - "\r*Highaltitude=?#\r"
    - "\r*standbynet=?#\r"

# Pull identity once on connect
on_connect:
  - "\r*modelname=?#\r"
  - "\r*macaddr=?#\r"

# ── Simulator ──
# One dispatcher script handler parses the *key=value grammar and
# handles every command, because the standby gate is stateful: a
# matched script handler always ends dispatch (there is no
# fall-through), so per-command handlers can't share a separate gate
# entry. Every reply echoes the received command first (mirroring real
# units) and terminates tokens with '#' — the driver frames on '#', so
# no trailing CR is needed. Step commands (vol=+, con=- ...) reply with
# the new absolute value; real units just echo the step, so state
# converges on the next poll there. In standby only power, identity,
# and standbynet answer; everything else gets *Block item# (an
# approximation of the per-model standby behavior).
simulator:
  initial_state:
    power: "off"
    source: hdmi
    volume: 5
    mute: false
    picture_mode: preset
    aspect: auto
    color_temp: normal
    contrast: 50
    brightness: 50
    color: 50
    sharpness: 15
    blank: false
    freeze: false
    light_mode: lnor
    light_level: 100
    light_hours: 342
    position: ft
    direct_power_on: "off"
    quick_auto_search: "off"
    high_altitude: "off"
    standby_network: "on"
    model_name: LK952
    mac_address: "80:65:e9:12:34:56"

  command_handlers:
    # Dispatcher: any *...# command. The simulator's line reader frames
    # incoming commands on CR/LF, so the trailing '#' is still present
    # here (unlike the driver side, which frames replies on '#').
    - match: '\*[^#]+#?'
      handler: |
        text = match.group(0).rstrip("#")
        body = text[1:]
        key, sep, val = body.partition("=")
        k = key.lower()
        v = val.lower() if sep else None
        echo = text + "#"

        BOOLS = {"mute": "mute", "blank": "blank", "freeze": "freeze"}
        ENUMS = {
            "sour": "source", "appmod": "picture_mode", "ct": "color_temp",
            "asp": "aspect", "lampm": "light_mode", "pp": "position",
            "directpower": "direct_power_on", "qas": "quick_auto_search",
            "highaltitude": "high_altitude", "standbynet": "standby_network",
        }
        INTS = {"vol": "volume", "lampcustom": "light_level"}
        STEPS = {"con": "contrast", "bri": "brightness", "color": "color", "sharp": "sharpness"}
        READS = {"ltim": "light_hours", "modelname": "model_name", "macaddr": "mac_address"}
        ACKS = ("menu", "up", "down", "left", "right", "enter", "auto",
                "lensload", "lenssave", "lensreset", "zoomi", "zoomo")
        STANDBY_OK = ("pow", "modelname", "macaddr", "standbynet")

        if state["power"] == "off" and k not in STANDBY_OK:
            respond(echo + "*Block item#")
        elif k == "pow":
            if v == "?":
                respond(echo + "*POW=" + str(state["power"]).upper() + "#")
            elif v in ("on", "off"):
                state["power"] = v
                respond(echo + "*POW=" + v.upper() + "#")
            else:
                respond(echo + "*Illegal format#")
        elif k in ENUMS:
            skey = ENUMS[k]
            if v == "?":
                respond(echo + "*" + k.upper() + "=" + str(state[skey]).upper() + "#")
            elif v:
                state[skey] = v
                respond(echo + "*" + k.upper() + "=" + v.upper() + "#")
            else:
                respond(echo + "*Illegal format#")
        elif k in BOOLS:
            skey = BOOLS[k]
            if v == "?":
                respond(echo + "*" + k.upper() + "=" + ("ON" if state[skey] else "OFF") + "#")
            elif v in ("on", "off"):
                state[skey] = (v == "on")
                respond(echo + "*" + k.upper() + "=" + v.upper() + "#")
            else:
                respond(echo + "*Illegal format#")
        elif k in INTS:
            skey = INTS[k]
            if v == "?":
                respond(echo + "*" + k.upper() + "=" + str(state[skey]) + "#")
            elif v in ("+", "-"):
                state[skey] = max(0, int(state[skey]) + (1 if v == "+" else -1))
                respond(echo + "*" + k.upper() + "=" + str(state[skey]) + "#")
            elif v is not None and v.isdigit():
                state[skey] = int(v)
                respond(echo + "*" + k.upper() + "=" + str(state[skey]) + "#")
            else:
                respond(echo + "*Illegal format#")
        elif k in STEPS:
            skey = STEPS[k]
            if v == "?":
                respond(echo + "*" + k.upper() + "=" + str(state[skey]) + "#")
            elif v in ("+", "-"):
                state[skey] = int(state[skey]) + (1 if v == "+" else -1)
                respond(echo + "*" + k.upper() + "=" + str(state[skey]) + "#")
            else:
                respond(echo + "*Unsupported item#")
        elif k in READS:
            if v == "?":
                respond(echo + "*" + k.upper() + "=" + str(state[READS[k]]) + "#")
            else:
                respond(echo + "*Unsupported item#")
        elif k in ACKS:
            respond(echo)
        else:
            respond(echo + "*Unsupported item#")

    # Garbage without the *...# grammar answers Illegal format.
    - match: '[\s\S]+'
      handler: |
        respond("*Illegal format#")
